EEVEE: precompile the shadow pipeline with one viewport without multi-viewport.

Blender-owned file; the hunk is enclosed in "UPBGE - Android" comments.
Not Android specific: affects any device without multiViewport.

The MAT_PIPE_SHADOW pipeline state hard-codes 16 viewports, but ShadowModule
only uses multi-viewport when GPU_multi_viewport_support() is true and
otherwise renders through one viewport. On Mali (maxViewports 1) the
precompiled pipeline violated VUID-VkPipelineViewportStateCreateInfo-
viewportCount-01216/01218 and never matched the runtime pipeline key anyway.

Applies after 0003.

diff --git a/source/blender/draw/engines/eevee/eevee_shader.cc b/source/blender/draw/engines/eevee/eevee_shader.cc
index 7b52346..ddd943c 100644
--- a/source/blender/draw/engines/eevee/eevee_shader.cc
+++ b/source/blender/draw/engines/eevee/eevee_shader.cc
@@ -1877,7 +1877,10 @@ void ShaderModule::material_create_info_pipelines_amend(eMaterialGeometry geomet
                  GPU_STENCIL_NONE,
                  GPU_STENCIL_OP_NONE,
                  GPU_VERTEX_LAST)
-          .viewports(16);
+          /* UPBGE - Android: without multi-viewport (Mali: maxViewports 1) shadows render
+           * through a single viewport (see ShadowModule), so must the precompiled state. */
+          .viewports(GPU_multi_viewport_support() ? 16 : 1);
+          /* UPBGE - Android */
       break;
     }
 
